gned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-14{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -14 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one), so ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{7}{4}{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our orthogonal complement is\n\n$$\n{H}^{⊥}=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512968 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186512989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512968 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "26a546ba-54ab-5cc8-83e6-b006c83a2260" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512968 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512989 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186513013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512989 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5ab17b99-dd7c-5473-a02e-1887d75473a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512989 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512990 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6102b09c-519b-52a5-908c-ac2692fae51a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512990 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186512878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513013 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186513014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513013 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b50cddb9-32fe-5feb-88b9-dbdd94647008" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513013 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186348409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513014 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186512990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513014 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b668892f-4bf5-5939-a70a-e3c5d414340b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218651301